@startuml
title Non-Functional Study - Interoperability, Scalability, Cost, Security

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontColor #1F2937
skinparam packageBorderColor #374151
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #F9FAFB
skinparam componentBorderColor #374151
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
skinparam arrowColor #374151

left to right direction

note as Purpose
  Purpose:
  Summarizes the main non-functional design considerations for
  the documentation phase. It explains how the selected ESP32,
  MQTT, local sensor wiring, and optional RS485 path affect
  interoperability, scalability, cost, and security.
end note

component "Recommended Core Design\nESP32 per machine + local wired sensors + MQTT over Wi-Fi" as Core

package "Interoperability" {
  component "Use standard MQTT topics\nfactory/{machineId}/telemetry" as I1
  component "Tag every record with\nmachineId, sensorId, timestamp" as I2
  component "Keep sensor interfaces documented\n1-Wire, I2C, SPI, UART" as I3
  component "Gateway can be local PC,\nRaspberry Pi, or cloud broker" as I4
}

package "Scalability" {
  component "Repeat one ESP32 node\nfor each new machine" as S1
  component "Topic naming separates\nmachine data streams" as S2
  component "Local buffering handles\nbrief network loss" as S3
  component "RS485/Modbus path for\nfuture industrial field bus" as S4
}

package "Cost" {
  component "ESP32 is low cost and\nhas built-in Wi-Fi" as C1
  component "Prototype sensors are affordable\nDS18B20 + ADXL345/MPU6050" as C2
  component "One node per machine costs more\nthan one central ESP32" as C3
  component "Lower wiring complexity can\nreduce installation effort" as C4
}

package "Security" {
  component "Use Wi-Fi credentials and\nseparate factory network" as Sec1
  component "Use MQTT username/password\nand TLS where supported" as Sec2
  component "Restrict dashboard access\nby user role" as Sec3
  component "Validate incoming telemetry\nbefore storage/analysis" as Sec4
}

Core --> I1
Core --> I2
Core --> I3
Core --> I4
Core --> S1
Core --> S2
Core --> S3
Core --> S4
Core --> C1
Core --> C2
Core --> C3
Core --> C4
Core --> Sec1
Core --> Sec2
Core --> Sec3
Core --> Sec4

legend bottom
|= Area |= What it evaluates |
| Interoperability | Whether sensors, ESP32 nodes, gateway, and cloud can exchange data through clear standards |
| Scalability | How easily the design grows from one machine to many machines |
| Cost | Hardware, wiring, setup, and maintenance effort tradeoffs |
| Security | Protection for device access, network traffic, dashboard use, and stored data |
| Core design | The recommended documentation baseline used by all diagrams |
endlegend
@enduml
